35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,I've found that charging money can actually alienate people and make them stop participating in the community.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I saw that people are having to move other bikes just to leave, and some spots get quite wet in the rain. It's a bit sad.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Our building account is practically empty, but the station park is expensive and full. There's definitely a demand for guaranteed spots.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"Adding more billing will increase the treasurer's workload significantly. Also, those fancy double-tier racks require physical maintenance and effort to use.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I was right! The same people have had the best spots for five years without any review. Plus, daily riders are actually okay with paying!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, if we charge, we risk the same isolation the neighboring block experienced. We should avoid creating ""debtors"" among us.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, it sounds like the current way isn't very fair. But we must be gentle about how we change it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, but if people are willing to pay for the convenience, why not use that to help the building's empty account?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, someone has to do the bookkeeping. Three hours a month is already a lot for a volunteer. We can't just add more.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"But the daily riders said they'd prefer paying over a ""one person, one claim"" rule! That's a huge hint, right?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, that might be true for some, but the complaint log shows that vague ownership leads to unresolved frustration.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"If we have a lottery, it might be fair, but will it solve the problem of bikes blocking each other?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"A lottery doesn't bring in any money. If we have a paid system, we can actually afford to fix the rain exposure issues.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,I'm still wary. A lottery is simple to run once a year. A paid system is a monthly headache.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I just want it to be fair! If the same people always have the dry spots, it's not fair.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I think we need a balance between fairness and maintaining our neighborly bonds.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let's see what the options are. I hope we can find a way that makes everyone smile.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I'm leaning towards something that reflects the actual value of the spaces.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,I'll support whatever is the least burdensome to maintain.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,As long as it's not the same people getting the best spots forever!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
