60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A is too risky for our community harmony. Option B sounds chaotic and physically difficult. I prefer Option C.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option B sounds like it might be hard for some of us to lift the bikes. A lottery seems fair and kind to all.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that makes financial sense. It rewards those who value the space and helps the building.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,Option B requires greasing and physical effort. Option A is a bookkeeping nightmare. Option C is the most efficient.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is interesting because daily riders like it, but Option C finally breaks the five-year streak of the same people winning!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the neighboring block's experience shows that Option A can lead to people avoiding meetings. Is the money worth that?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, do you think a lottery would stop the shoving matches in the morning?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, we can set a reasonable price. It's better than having no funds for the building at all.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, the treasurer is already spending three hours a month. We cannot add more billing tasks to that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, maybe not entirely, but at least everyone knows they have a fair chance at a good spot every year!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm sticking with C. It's a clean slate every year and doesn't create financial tension.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Misaki. Option C is the most peaceful way to handle this.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I still think we're missing a huge opportunity for the building's budget, but I see the consensus forming.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"Option C is the only one that doesn't create a permanent, exhausting chore for the association.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm torn, but the ""fairness"" of a lottery is better than the current stagnation. I'll go with C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,It seems we are mostly in agreement.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It's lovely when we can all find a middle ground.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, I'll concede. But we should discuss a separate levy for the rain covers later!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,Agreed. Let's keep it simple.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"Yay! Finally, a change!","{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
